cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "HandoverLab: system-level handover simulator for 5G-Advanced and beyond-5G research"
abstract: >-
  HandoverLab is an open-source, system-level simulator of 3GPP mobility procedures (baseline
  handover with Event A3, Release-16 conditional and DAPS handover, Release-18 L1/L2-triggered
  mobility, conditional handover with the location events of Release 18) for many users in dense
  5G and beyond-5G networks, on a street grid, in an open area, along a highway, indoors, in rural
  cells, along a high-speed railway or under the earth-moving beams of a LEO satellite. It provides a
  TR 38.901 received-power radio model (TR 38.811 for the satellite) with optional TDL fast fading,
  SSB and UE receive beams, several carriers and dual connectivity, an optional slot scheduler with
  MCS, TBS and HARQ and user-plane buffers at handover, an L3-filtered measurement chain, a
  radio-link failure model, an outcome label for every handover attempt, a plug-in interface for
  handover rules (including a measurement-prediction rule after TR 38.744), equal-budget tuning
  studies with paired statistics, and verification against hand-computed values, golden event-log
  fingerprints, the 3GPP large-scale calibration and ns-3 / 5G-LENA.
